.SH NAME
.PP
auto-set-hostname - Permanently set a new hostname

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-set-hostname new-hostname
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
new-hostname    The new hostname for the system
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-set-hostname
command provides a platform-independent interface for permanently
changing the hostname of the system.  Native interfaces for changing
the hostname vary widely across operating systems, creating
hurdles for those who want to automate management of
multiple different systems.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-set-hostname myhost.mydomain
.ad
.fi

